From: Jaime Dias <jaimejosediasnt@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 16:15:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Initialize the secondary machine read value

The page-fault decoder always carries two result slots because 128-bit loads
need both.  A machine-handled narrow read returns before the ordinary load
switch initializes the second one, so initialize it at the machine boundary.
---
 src/aarch64/vectors.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/aarch64/vectors.c b/src/aarch64/vectors.c
--- a/src/aarch64/vectors.c
+++ b/src/aarch64/vectors.c
@@ -825,6 +825,7 @@ int SYSReadValFromAddr(uint64_t *value, uint64_t *value2, int size, uint64_t far)
     D(kprintf("[JIT:SYS] SYSReadValFromAddr(%d, %p)\n", size, far));
 
 #ifdef BELLATRIX_EMU68
+    *value2 = 0;
     if (machine_bus_read((uint32_t)far, size, value))
         return 1;
 #endif
